/target

# Where the packaging workflows render their templates, and where makepkg
# leaves what it builds. The templates under packaging/ are the source; what
# lands here is derived from a published release and is regenerated, never
# edited. Ignored so that rendering one locally to test it cannot be committed.
/build
/assets

# Zensical documentation build output
site/

# Coverage output
lcov.info

# --- mise ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A common global gitignore (`~/.config/git/ignore`) excludes `mise.toml`,
# `mise.*.toml` and `mise.lock`, on the assumption that mise configuration is a
# personal thing. Here it is not: `mise.toml` defines the project's tasks and
# `mise.lock` pins every tool to an exact build, which is what makes
# `mise run ci` locally and the CI workflow run the same versions. Both are
# re-included explicitly so the repository does not depend on how any one
# developer has configured Git.
#
# A repository `.gitignore` takes precedence over `core.excludesFile`, so these
# negations do the job.
!mise.toml
!mise.lock

# Genuinely local, and genuinely per-developer: overrides and secrets that must
# not be shared. Already covered by the global `mise.*.toml`, but stated here so
# the intent survives a developer who has no global ignore at all.
mise.local.toml
